Package: JM4QTN
Type: Package
Title: Joint Mapping for Quantitative Trait Nucleotides (QTN)
Version: 2.0.0
Date: 2025-08-13
Author: Junhui Li, Wenxin Liu
Maintainer: Junhui Li <junhuili@cau.edu.cn>
Description: A comprehensive R package for joint mapping analysis of quantitative trait 
    nucleotides (QTN) in genetic studies. The package implements sophisticated statistical 
    methods for both Association Mapping (AM) and Linkage Mapping (LM) approaches to 
    identify QTL affecting multiple traits simultaneously. Key features include: Joint 
    mapping analysis for multiple traits using multivariate models, permutation testing 
    for empirical significance threshold determination, linkage-pleiotropy analysis to 
    distinguish between pleiotropic and linked QTL effects, missing genotype imputation 
    using flanking marker information, virtual marker creation for improved mapping 
    resolution, comprehensive statistical analysis including normality tests, ANOVA, 
    and least squares means, support for various population types (F2, RIL, DH, 
    backcross, advanced generations), stepwise regression with multiple information 
    criteria for cofactor selection, and parametric bootstrap testing for hypothesis 
    testing. The package combines composite interval mapping (CIM) and regression 
    analysis to perform association mapping and linkage mapping, identifying pleiotropic 
    or linked QTL in multiple traits across single or multiple line cross populations. 
    It can compute conditional probabilities of missing marker genotypes using flanking 
    markers and determine significance thresholds through permutation tests and 
    parametric bootstrap tests.
License: GPL (>= 2)
Imports: lsmeans (>= 2.25.5), StepReg (>= 1.0.1)
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
